## Emergency Procedures

### Complete System Failure

```bash
# 1. Stop all services
docker-compose down

# 2. Check system resources
df -h  # Disk space
free -h  # Memory
top  # CPU usage

# 3. Clean Docker
docker system prune -a --volumes

# 4. Restore from backup
./scripts/deploy.sh production --rollback

# 5. Start with fresh deployment
./scripts/deploy.sh production --build --migrate
```

### Database Corruption

```bash
# 1. Stop application
docker-compose stop app

# 2. Export data
docker-compose exec mongodb mongodump \
  --db=ai_receptionist \
  --out=/tmp/backup

# 3. Repair database
docker-compose exec mongodb mongosh
> use ai_receptionist
> db.repairDatabase()

# 4. If repair fails, restore from backup
docker-compose exec mongodb mongorestore \
  --db=ai_receptionist \
  /path/to/backup/ai_receptionist

# 5. Restart
docker-compose up -d
```

### Security Incident

```bash
# 1. Immediately revoke compromised API keys
# Update GOOGLE_API_KEY in .env

# 2. Rotate all secrets
# Generate new API_KEY, database passwords

# 3. Check logs for suspicious activity
grep "401\|403\|500" logs/ai_receptionist.log

# 4. Review access logs
docker-compose logs nginx | grep -E "POST|DELETE"

# 5. Update and redeploy
./scripts/deploy.sh production --build --backup
```

